docs/controls.md:51:- C12 - A loaded completed snapshot keeps the win banner static and plays no celebration. Import doesn't write a best score. Resuming an unfinished snapshot and later winning records a local best under R10.
docs/controls.md:63:Run `npm run --silent replay -- PATH` to read a replay file. On valid input, print only the final snapshot JSON to stdout and exit 0. On invalid input, print nothing to stdout, write a message to stderr and exit nonzero.
docs/controls.md:65:## Deal names
docs/controls.md:67:- C15.1 - Add a native text input labelled "Deal name" inside the reproduction controls. Start empty. Limit a name to 40 UTF-16 code units and reject carriage returns and line feeds. Keep all other characters and surrounding spaces unchanged.
docs/controls.md:68:- C15.2 - Editing a name leaves the board code, cards, moves, clock and pause unchanged. Allow editing while paused or completed. Clearing the field makes the game unnamed.
docs/controls.md:69:- C15.3 - Export named progress as version 2 and unnamed progress as version 1, as D05 defines.
docs/controls.md:70:- C15.4 - A named import restores its name with C09 and C10's pause behavior. A version 1 import clears the name. Importing completed named progress keeps C12's static banner and best-score rules.
docs/controls.md:71:- C15.5 - New Game, Restart, size changes and board-code loads clear the name. Names aren't saved in browser preferences. Reload follows R08 and starts an unnamed fresh deal.
