docs/input.md:49:## Card names
docs/input.md:51:The button names describe the information available to the player:
docs/input.md:54:- I15 - Name a revealed or matched card by its position, face name and state. Use the face names defined in [Visuals](visuals.md).
docs/input.md:56:For example, the first hidden button is named "Row 1, column 1, closed". Once revealed, its name includes the face, so a player can remember it without seeing the drawing.
docs/input.md:77:- I17 - Support a complete 4x4 keyboard game with a screen reader. Find Grid size and New Game by name, enter the board, expose closed positions and revealed faces by name and state, announce one result per turn and make the win, final moves and time available. Leave the board with Tab and start another game. Deliver automated accessibility-tree evidence for this journey. Record the browser and tool versions in the project README and say whether a screen reader was used. If one was used, record its name and version. The user confirms spoken output during acceptance. Spoken confirmation isn't the developer's deliverable.
docs/acceptance.md:33:Check [Reproducibility](reproducibility.md) with its example deck and replay. Check snapshot round trips and malformed input. Check the exact mismatch timeout before an equal-time replay action.
docs/acceptance.md:35:Load an unfinished snapshot, attempt input while paused, then Resume. Check its remaining active time and focus. Load a completed snapshot and check its static banner and unchanged best score.
docs/README.md:14:Use mouse, touch or keyboard for the same card action. Keyboard movement, focus, card names and the screen reader journey are in [Input](input.md). The labels and behavior of game and reproduction actions are in [Controls](controls.md).
docs/README.md:22:A board code describes a deal. A snapshot saves progress. A replay records timed actions. Unnamed snapshots, board codes and replays keep format version 1. Named snapshots use version 2. The algorithms and formats are in [Reproducibility](reproducibility.md).
