docs/reproducibility.md:6:A board code reproduces the starting cards. A snapshot restores a later position. A replay shows the actions that produced a position, so each format answers a different debugging question.
docs/reproducibility.md:26:- D05 - Encode unnamed progress as a version 1 JSON object with exactly `version`, `boardCode`, `matched`, `selection`, `moves`, `elapsedMs` and `started`. Encode named progress as version 2 with those fields plus `name`. Version 2 requires a nonempty string name that follows C15. Version 1 has no name field. Accept both versions on import and reject every other version. The CLI still accepts version 1 replays and emits their unnamed version 1 snapshots. `matched` is an array of matched position indices. Derive the deck, pair count and completion from these fields.
